  "passage": {
    "text": "Farming is a risky business because farmers depend on the weather. Last summer there was a drought. It did not rain for six weeks, and the crops did not grow well. The yield was smaller than in other years, so farmers had less to sell and lower incomes. This year there is too much rain, and that also damages the crops. Some farmers buy insurance. When a disaster happens, the insurance company pays them compensation. Other farmers grow several different crops. If one crop fails, they still have the others.",
